<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss money market rates seen steady.</title>
<headline>Swiss money market rates seen steady.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss money market rates were seen fairly steady in early trade, with one bank quoting tomorrow/next money at 1-7/16 to 1-1/2 percent.</p>
<p>Traders said the Swiss National Bank (SNB) added some funds to the market in routine morning operations.</p>
<p>The funds were said to be priced at 1-7/16 percent, and were for the period from October 7 to 10, and from October 8 to 14.</p>
<p>Activity was quiet, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
